# trust-ladder.yml — the explicit, Captain-authored trust ladder.
#
# THE earn_up SURFACE ONLY (axes spec 2026-07-05 §1 L1). This file is consulted
# exclusively when instance/config/posture.yml (or the CABINET_POSTURE narrow
# env/file) resolves the `earn_up` posture — guardian and sovereign never read
# it. load-preset.sh materializes this example to trust-ladder.yml on a fresh
# hatch ONLY when that file is absent. If ABSENT or corrupt, the conservative
# default is a single `would-like-to` rung (propose everything, lift nothing)
# — the safe floor. THIS EXAMPLE SHIPS EXACTLY THAT FLOOR, stated explicitly,
# plus commented synthetic examples (Testburg lanes) showing how a ladder
# grows. Nothing here grants any autonomy by itself.
#
# This is the Captain-readable map of NAMED rungs a lane climbs as cells prove
# out. It sits ABOVE the per-cell graduation machine
# (framework/fidelity/graduation.py) and the authority matrix
# (framework/policies/authority-matrix.yml) — it does not replace either: the
# static postures.earn_up table floors every non-ceiling class at propose_only,
# and ALL autonomy above that floor comes from this ladder at run time.
#
# RUNG VOCABULARY + the FROZEN rung → verdict map the gate overlay lifts a
# graduated, rung-granted cell to. Lowest to highest; you may use any subset,
# in this order, per lane:
#   would-like-to    propose-first (waits for approval)      -> propose_only  [the floor]
#   intend-to        veto-window (announces, acts unless vetoed) -> auto_with_veto_window
#   ive-done         acts, reports after                     -> notify_after
#   ive-been-doing   fully graduated (acts, reports periodically) -> auto
#
# HOW A RUNG IS EARNED: every (lane, action_type) cell the rung `grants` must
# be `graduated` per graduation.evaluate (the proof bar is the matrix `bars`,
# not a second bar). An earned rung is SURFACED as a one-tap card — it is
# NEVER auto-granted; there is no self-grant path in code. You grant it by
# appending a `granted:` row to THIS file in an unlock window (sudo bash
# cabinet/scripts/germline-lock.sh unlock instance/config/trust-ladder.yml →
# edit → re-lock; trust_ladder.grant_rung then records the trust_rung_granted
# AUDIT event). The ATTESTED (Captain-locked) file is the ONLY authority
# source — `granted:` rows in an unlocked file are ignored, and a bare
# trust_rung_granted event mints nothing (the ledger is same-uid-appendable).
# Only a locked-file granted row advances the ladder, and only then do
# GRADUATED cells on that lane resolve to the rung's verdict above.
#
# THIS FILE IS ALSO THE LIFT CAP: the gate overlay lifts at most to the
# highest rung this file still defines for the lane (min of granted rung and
# file cap). Deleting or corrupting this file drops every lift back to the
# propose_only floor — your mechanical kill handle for the earn_up surface.
#
# HARD CEILING: if any granted cell's action_type maps to a hard-ceiling
# risk_class (external_comms, deploy_prod, spend, secrets, network_write,
# credentials_grant), the rung is computed as Captain-only — the ladder will
# NEVER auto-advance past it, and the gate overlay never lifts a ceiling row
# regardless of rung (ceilings stay always_gated in the earn_up table). You
# can still grant such a rung explicitly, but it stays your decision forever.
# This is enforced in code, not just here.

rungs:
  # --- THE FLOOR (the shipped default) -------------------------------------
  # One base rung, every lane: propose everything, lift nothing. This is
  # byte-equivalent to the fail-closed default an absent file resolves to —
  # written out so the materialized file SHOWS the real day-one state.
  - name: would-like-to
    lane: null                     # null = every lane
    grants: []                     # the floor grants nothing

  # --- SYNTHETIC EXAMPLES (Testburg lanes) — uncomment + rename to grow ----
  # - name: ive-done               # graduated cells act, report after (notify_after)
  #   lane: testburg-market
  #   grants:
  #     - { action_type: task_status_move }   # board/task status moves
  #     - { action_type: board_status }
  #     - { action_type: label }
  #     - { action_type: tier2_note }
  #   # min_samples is OPTIONAL — omit to use the matrix `bars` floor (20 for
  #   # `default`). Set it to require MORE proof than the matrix floor for
  #   # this specific rung.
  #   # min_samples: 30
  #
  # - name: intend-to              # internal comms with a veto window
  #   lane: testburg-market
  #   grants:
  #     - { action_type: internal_message }
  #     - { action_type: internal_email }
  #   min_samples: 30              # internal_comms bar is already 30 in the matrix
  #
  # - name: ive-done               # a second lane climbs separately (trust is per-lane)
  #   lane: testburg-harbor
  #   grants:
  #     - { action_type: task_status_move }
  #     - { action_type: board_status }
  #
  # A CEILING rung, shown for documentation: computed Captain-only
  # (external_message -> external_comms ceiling). The ladder will surface it
  # when the cell graduates, but will NEVER auto-advance to it, and the gate
  # overlay never lifts the external_comms row.
  # - name: ive-done
  #   lane: testburg-market
  #   grants:
  #     - { action_type: external_message }   # -> external_comms (HARD CEILING)

# --- GRANTED ROWS — the Captain's actual grants (closed shape) -------------
# Authority lives HERE, in the locked file — never in events. Each row:
#   rung        required, one of the four vocabulary names above
#   lane        optional — absent/null applies to EVERY lane
#   granted_at  optional provenance timestamp
#   note        optional free text
# Malformed rows (unknown keys, out-of-vocab rung) are line-dropped
# fail-closed. The effective lift per lane = min(highest applicable granted
# row, highest rung the `rungs:` map still defines for the lane).
#
# granted:
#   - { rung: ive-done, lane: testburg-market, granted_at: 2026-07-09, note: "example" }

# NOTE (deliberate absence): the pre-ripout `auto_grant_nonceiling` flag does
# NOT exist anymore. Every rung — ceiling or not — is grant-by-Captain only;
# the resurrected module ships no auto-advance path at all (axes Corridor
# constraint: authority changes ride Captain-authenticated surfaces only).
